# Phase 18 factory per-client NameServer refresh schedules

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 09:56:28 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Implementation revision: `681a8acf`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: `MQClientAPIFactory` periodic NameServer discovery schedule

## Finding and change

Pinned Java `createAndStart` schedules one `fetchNameServerAddr` fixed-rate
task per API client, with a 10-second initial delay and a 120-second period.
Rust previously used one timer worker that fetched each pool slot sequentially.
Rust now owns one Tokio refresh task per pool slot, applies each result only to
that slot, uses fixed-rate missed-tick catch-up, and signals and joins all
tasks during factory shutdown.

The invoked Java factory fixture uses a `ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor` and
captures two scheduled registrations after starting two domain clients. It
also preserves the distinct lookup results `127.0.0.11:9876` and
`127.0.0.12:9876`. A paused-time Rust regression checks its per-slot task
count against the fixture and verifies distinct refreshed results after the
first 10-second tick.

